; SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
;
; Node — the syntax tree, ported from the reference's internal/ast/ast.go and
; ast_generated.go.
;
; ── The shape, and why it is this one (CLAUDE.md §3.1) ──────────────────────
;
; The reference's Node is a tag-struct with an INTERFACE payload:
;
;     type Node struct { Kind Kind; Flags NodeFlags; Loc TextRange; data nodeData }
;
; where `nodeData` has ~20 methods and 168 concrete implementations. Here the
; interface becomes a SUM TYPE — `NodeData union` — and every dispatch is a
; `choose`. The reason is not taste: a trait object makes the callee unknown at
; compile time, and purity, escape and parallelism analysis all stop at that
; point. Upstream says the same thing from the other side at Node.IterChildren
; ("an interface call is opaque to escape analysis").
;
; The SPLIT is kept exactly as the reference has it — kind/flags/pos/end beside
; the payload, not folded into the union. That is load-bearing rather than
; imitative: many KINDS share one payload. Every punctuation and keyword token
; node is a `Token` with no fields at all, so a union arm per kind would be 100+
; empty arms and the kind would still have to be stored to tell them apart.
;
; ★ ORDER-OF-DECLARATION AUFLAGE, inherited from dazzle's `Insn union`: the tag
; IS the jump-table index, and AArch64's MinimumJumpTableEntries is 13 — a
; dispatch level needs >= 14 CONTIGUOUS tags or LLVM lowers a compare chain
; instead. That does not bite yet (this slice has twelve arms and every choose
; over them is cold), but the union only grows, and the arms that end up on the
; hot path must be contiguous when it does. Do not reorder for tidiness.
;
; ── What is carried ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; Slices 1–2: SourceFile, the bare Token, Identifier, the literal kinds, and the
; statements a file of declarations and expressions is made of. Slice 3 adds the
; TYPE surface — the alias declaration, type parameters, references and
; qualified names, unions and intersections, the postfix and bracketed forms,
; tuples, conditional and infer types, and the predicates. Slice 4 adds the
; SIGNATURE — the parameter, the function declaration, the function and
; constructor types, and the two statements a function BODY is made of that a
; file of declarations never needed: `return` and `if`. Slice 5 adds the
; EXPRESSION ladder: the binary and conditional operators, the unary and update
; forms, member/element access and calls, `as`/`satisfies`, the parenthesized,
; array and object literals, `new`, the function expression and the arrow
; function. Slice 6 adds the CLASS family — the declaration and the expression,
; the heritage clauses, and the six member forms (method, property,
; constructor, get/set accessor, static block, index signature). Slice 7 adds
; the TYPE-MEMBER surface — the object type literal and the five member forms
; an interface body is made of, the mapped type, and the interface, enum and
; module declarations. Slice 8 adds the IMPORT and EXPORT declarations, which
; is parseDeclarationWorker's last two arms and therefore the last of the
; router. Slice 9 adds the LOOP and BRANCH statements — `do`, `while`, the
; three `for` heads, `break`/`continue`, `with`, `switch` with its case block
; and clauses, `throw`, `try`/`catch`/`finally`, `debugger`, and the labeled
; statement that `break outer` exists for. Slice 10 adds the BINDING PATTERN,
; slice 11 the TEMPLATE family, and slice 12 the DECORATOR — ONE arm, because a
; decorator is an element of the same `modifiers` list a keyword goes into and
; needed no new slot on any node that carries one.
;
; Everything else is not a missing arm here — it is a construct the parser
; reports as unported before it ever gets to build a node.
;
; ★ The union is now 134 arms, and the AUFLAGE above starts to bite: the arms
; that end up on a hot path must be CONTIGUOUS. Nothing here is hot yet (the
; only consumer is a debug walk), so no order is being defended — but the next
; reader to add an arm should add it at the END rather than "where it belongs
; alphabetically", so that a later regrouping is one deliberate move instead of
; an archaeology exercise.
;
; ★ Three node kinds deliberately have NO arm of their own: OmittedExpression,
; the zero-width placeholder an array literal's elision leaves behind (`[, 1]`),
; SemicolonClassElement, the stray `;` between class members, and (slice 9)
; DebuggerStatement. None of the three carries a field or a child, so each is a
; `Token` whose KIND says which it is — the same reasoning KeywordTypeNode and
; ThisTypeNode are Tokens under.
;
; NOT carried, and each omission is a decision rather than an oversight:
;
;   - `Parent`. The reference sets it in a pass AFTER ParseSourceFile
;     (setParentFromContext), so there is nothing to compare and nothing to port
;     yet. Under RBMM the back-pointer costs nothing when it comes — a cycle
;     inside one region is freed with the region.
;   - The node ID. It is assigned deterministically at parse time here, not
;     lazily by CAS into the shared tree (CLAUDE.md §3.10) — but nothing reads
;     one yet, so the field waits for its first reader.
;   - The identifier/literal TEXT. The reference stores scanner.TokenValue().
;     Our scanner keeps no tokenValue (its own header says why), and the
;     yardstick compares spans rather than text, so the field is deferred to the
;     slice that first needs it — which is the one that has to tell `let` used
;     as a keyword from `let` used as a name.

use scaly.memory.Page
use scaly.containers.Array
use tscaly.Diagnostics.DiagnosticList

; ── per-kind payload records ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; One record per reference struct, named for it. A record with no fields is not
; a placeholder: the reference's Token and EmptyStatement have none either.

define TokenData ()
define IdentifierData ()
define LiteralData ()
define EmptyStatementData ()

define SourceFileData
(
    statements: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    end_of_file_token: pointer[AstNode]

    ; The reference's `result.SetDiagnostics(...)` in finishSourceFile. The
    ; parser accumulates into this list during the parse and hands it over at the
    ; end, which is also what makes the list readable from a program ROOT: a
    ; generic instance handed across a package boundary reads back as garbage
    ; (root CLAUDE.md), so the dump asks AstNode for it through statics, exactly
    ; as it asks for children.
    ;
    ; ★ NOT a child. It is absent from this arm's slot list in child_at below,
    ; because ForEachChild does not visit diagnostics — adding it there would put
    ; a diagnostic in the tree walk and every case would diverge.
    diagnostics: pointer[DiagnosticList]
)

define BlockData (statements: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]])

define ExpressionStatementData (expression: pointer[AstNode])

define VariableStatementData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    declaration_list: pointer[AstNode]
)

define VariableDeclarationListData (declarations: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]])

; The expression is OPTIONAL — a bare `return;` has none — which is why this is
; not ExpressionStatementData under another arm name despite the identical slot
; list: the two records differ in what null MEANS, and that difference is the
; kind of thing a shared record hides.
define ReturnStatementData (expression: pointer[AstNode])

define IfStatementData
(
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
    then_statement: pointer[AstNode]
    else_statement: pointer[AstNode]
)

define VariableDeclarationData
(
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    exclamation_token: pointer[AstNode]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
    initializer: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ── the type surface (parser slice 3) ───────────────────────────────────────
;
; ★ TWO reference node types need NO record of their own, and saying so is
; cheaper than a comment on each absence:
;
;   KeywordTypeNode  — `string`, `number`, `any`, `void`, … It carries nothing
;                      but its KIND, which is the keyword's own kind, and the
;                      kind lives beside the payload rather than in it (see the
;                      header). So it is a `Token`, exactly as a punctuation
;                      node is.
;   ThisTypeNode     — likewise: kind KindThisType, no fields, no children.
;
; Several arms deliberately SHARE a record. `WrappedTypeData` is the reference's
; recurring one-child type node under one name; the ARM tells the kinds apart,
; and the kind is what the yardstick compares. Grouping them is not a
; simplification of the reference — each of these structs really does have
; exactly one child slot, and the arm names keep them individually visible.

define WrappedTypeData (inner: pointer[AstNode])

define TypeListData (types: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]])

define QualifiedNameData
(
    left: pointer[AstNode]
    right: pointer[AstNode]
)

define TypeReferenceData
(
    type_name: pointer[AstNode]
    type_arguments: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
)

define TypeQueryData
(
    expr_name: pointer[AstNode]
    type_arguments: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
)

define IndexedAccessTypeData
(
    object_type: pointer[AstNode]
    index_type: pointer[AstNode]
)

define ConditionalTypeData
(
    check_type: pointer[AstNode]
    extends_type: pointer[AstNode]
    true_type: pointer[AstNode]
    false_type: pointer[AstNode]
)

define TypePredicateData
(
    asserts_modifier: pointer[AstNode]
    parameter_name: pointer[AstNode]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
)

define NamedTupleMemberData
(
    dot_dot_dot_token: pointer[AstNode]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    question_token: pointer[AstNode]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
)

define TypeParameterData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    constraint: pointer[AstNode]
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
    default_type: pointer[AstNode]
)

define TypeAliasDeclarationData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    type_parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ── signatures (parser slice 4) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; The reference's ParameterDeclaration, FunctionDeclaration, FunctionTypeNode
; and ConstructorTypeNode. They share the SIGNATURE shape — type parameters,
; parameters, return type — and they are separate records anyway, because the
; slots around that shape differ and the slot ORDER is what the yardstick
; compares.

define ParameterData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    dot_dot_dot_token: pointer[AstNode]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    question_token: pointer[AstNode]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
    initializer: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ★ The reference has a slot this record does not: `FullSignature`, visited
; between `Type` and `Body`. It is only ever non-nil for a JSDoc reparse — the
; parse path passes nil at its single construction site — so it is left out
; rather than carried as a field nothing can ever fill. The slice that ports
; the JSDoc reparser adds it, and its place in the child order is HERE, before
; the body.
define FunctionDeclarationData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    asterisk_token: pointer[AstNode]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    type_parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
    body: pointer[AstNode]
)

define FunctionTypeData
(
    type_parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
)

define ConstructorTypeData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    type_parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ── the expression ladder (parser slice 5) ──────────────────────────────────
;
; ★ THREE reference structs carry a slot this port does not, and all three are
; nil on the PARSE path — they exist for the JSDoc reparser, which builds a
; BinaryExpression / PropertyAssignment / ShorthandPropertyAssignment with a
; type annotation that no source text can produce:
;
;   BinaryExpression              modifiers, Type   (NewBinaryExpression is
;                                                    called with nil for both)
;   PropertyAssignment            Type
;   ShorthandPropertyAssignment   Type
;
; Same treatment as FunctionDeclaration's FullSignature above: left out rather
; than carried as a field nothing can fill, and the place in the child order is
; named here so the JSDoc slice can put it back — Type sits BETWEEN Left and
; OperatorToken, and between the postfix token and what follows it.
;
; ★ ArrayLiteralExpression and ObjectLiteralExpression additionally carry a
; `MultiLine bool`. It is a plain FIELD, not a NodeFlag, so the yardstick cannot
; see it and nothing here reads one — stated rather than silently dropped,
; because a distinction the dump hides hides every bug in it.

define BinaryExpressionData
(
    left: pointer[AstNode]
    operator_token: pointer[AstNode]
    right: pointer[AstNode]
)

define ConditionalExpressionData
(
    condition: pointer[AstNode]
    question_token: pointer[AstNode]
    when_true: pointer[AstNode]
    colon_token: pointer[AstNode]
    when_false: pointer[AstNode]
)

; asteriskToken, expression — both optional, since a bare `yield;` has neither.
define YieldExpressionData
(
    asterisk_token: pointer[AstNode]
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
)

; AsExpression and SatisfiesExpression: expression, then type. Shared, and the
; ARM tells them apart — the same reasoning WrappedTypeData is shared under.
define AsExpressionData
(
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
)

; `<T>x`. The type comes FIRST here, which is the opposite of AsExpression and
; is exactly why the two do not share a record: the order is what the yardstick
; compares.
define TypeAssertionData
(
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
)

define PropertyAccessData
(
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
    question_dot_token: pointer[AstNode]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
)

define ElementAccessData
(
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
    question_dot_token: pointer[AstNode]
    argument_expression: pointer[AstNode]
)

define CallExpressionData
(
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
    question_dot_token: pointer[AstNode]
    type_arguments: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    arguments: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
)

define NewExpressionData
(
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
    type_arguments: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    arguments: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
)

define ExpressionWithTypeArgumentsData
(
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
    type_arguments: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
)

; The elements of an array literal and the properties of an object literal. A
; separate record from TypeListData above only because the two say different
; things about what they hold; both are one list and nothing else.
define ElementListData (elements: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]])

define ArrowFunctionData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    type_parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
    equals_greater_than_token: pointer[AstNode]
    body: pointer[AstNode]
)

define FunctionExpressionData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    asterisk_token: pointer[AstNode]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    type_parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
    body: pointer[AstNode]
)

define PropertyAssignmentData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    postfix_token: pointer[AstNode]
    initializer: pointer[AstNode]
)

define ShorthandPropertyAssignmentData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    postfix_token: pointer[AstNode]
    equals_token: pointer[AstNode]
    object_assignment_initializer: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ── the class family (parser slice 6) ───────────────────────────────────────

; ClassDeclaration and ClassExpression have the SAME slot list, in the same
; order, and the reference gives them one embedded ClassLikeBase for exactly
; that reason. The ARM tells them apart, as it does for AsExpression and
; SatisfiesExpression.
define ClassLikeData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    type_parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    heritage_clauses: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    members: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
)

; ★ `token` is the KEYWORD — KindExtendsKeyword or KindImplementsKeyword — and
; it is a field rather than a child: the reference stores it as a bare
; `Token ast.Kind` and its ForEachChild visits only Types. The node's own
; `kind` is KindHeritageClause for both, so without this field the two clauses
; would be indistinguishable. Nothing reads it yet and the yardstick cannot
; see it, but a clause that does not know which one it is is not a port of
; this node.
define HeritageClauseData
(
    token: int
    types: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
)

define MethodDeclarationData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    asterisk_token: pointer[AstNode]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    postfix_token: pointer[AstNode]
    type_parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
    body: pointer[AstNode]
)

define PropertyDeclarationData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    postfix_token: pointer[AstNode]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
    initializer: pointer[AstNode]
)

; A constructor has no NAME — `constructor` is the keyword, not an identifier
; node — which is the one thing that keeps this from being MethodDeclarationData.
define ConstructorDeclarationData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    type_parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
    body: pointer[AstNode]
)

; GetAccessorDeclaration and SetAccessorDeclaration, again one record and two
; arms: the reference's two ForEachChild bodies are slot-for-slot identical.
define AccessorDeclarationData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    type_parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
    body: pointer[AstNode]
)

define ClassStaticBlockDeclarationData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    body: pointer[AstNode]
)

define IndexSignatureDeclarationData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ── the type-member surface (parser slice 7) ────────────────────────────────
;
; An interface BODY and an object TYPE LITERAL are the same production —
; parseTypeMember, with its five member forms — which is why they are one
; slice and one set of records.

define TypeLiteralData (members: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]])

; CallSignature and ConstructSignature, one record and two arms: the
; reference's two ForEachChild bodies are slot-for-slot identical, and the
; `new` of a construct signature is a keyword rather than a child.
define SignatureDeclarationData
(
    type_parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ★ NOT MethodDeclarationData. The two field LISTS differ by an asterisk and a
; body, and it is tempting to reuse the record with both left null, because
; the visit order that comes out is then the same. It is the same by accident:
; a generator method signature is a grammar error the CHECKER reports, so the
; reference PARSES the asterisk in a class and refuses it here by having no
; slot for it. A shared record would give this node somewhere to put one.
define MethodSignatureData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    postfix_token: pointer[AstNode]
    type_parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    parameters: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
)

define EnumDeclarationData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    members: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
)

define EnumMemberData
(
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    initializer: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ★ `keyword` is KindNamespaceKeyword, KindModuleKeyword or KindGlobalKeyword,
; and it is a field rather than a child — the same shape HeritageClauseData's
; `token` has, for the same reason. All three spellings produce a node whose
; own `kind` is KindModuleDeclaration, so without this field `namespace A {}`
; and `module A {}` are indistinguishable. The yardstick cannot see it; a
; module that does not know which word declared it is not a port of this node.
define ModuleDeclarationData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    keyword: int
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    body: pointer[AstNode]
)

define MappedTypeData
(
    readonly_token: pointer[AstNode]
    type_parameter: pointer[AstNode]
    name_type: pointer[AstNode]
    question_token: pointer[AstNode]
    type_node: pointer[AstNode]
    members: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
)

; ── the import and export declarations (parser slice 8) ─────────────────────
;
; parseDeclarationWorker's two remaining arms. They are one slice because they
; are one production in three places: parseImportOrExportSpecifier builds
; `{ a as b }` for both sides, parseModuleSpecifier reads the `"mod"` for both,
; and parseImportAttributes reads the `with { … }` for both.

define ImportDeclarationData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    import_clause: pointer[AstNode]
    module_specifier: pointer[AstNode]
    attributes: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ★ `is_type_only` is a FIELD, not a child — the shape HeritageClauseData's
; `token` and ModuleDeclarationData's `keyword` have, and for the same reason:
; `import type A = require("m")` and `import A = require("m")` produce the same
; kind with the same children, so without the field the two are the same node.
define ImportEqualsDeclarationData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    is_type_only: bool
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    module_reference: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ★ `phase_modifier` is the reference's ImportPhaseModifierSyntaxKind —
; KindTypeKeyword, KindDeferKeyword, or KindUnknown for a plain import. A
; field, for the reason above.
define ImportClauseData
(
    phase_modifier: int
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    named_bindings: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ImportSpecifier and ExportSpecifier, one record and two arms — and this is
; the §3.5n check performed rather than assumed: the reference's two structs
; carry the SAME three slots in the same order (IsTypeOnly, PropertyName,
; name) and their two ForEachChild bodies are identical. The only difference
; is a Go TYPE — an import specifier's name is an IdentifierNode and an export
; specifier's a ModuleExportName, i.e. an identifier OR a string literal —
; which is a distinction the parser enforces at parse_import_specifier, not a
; slot this record would have to hold.
define ImportOrExportSpecifierData
(
    is_type_only: bool
    property_name: pointer[AstNode]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ★ `token` is KindWithKeyword or KindAssertKeyword: `with { type: "json" }`
; and the deprecated `assert { … }` are the same node under different words,
; so the word is the only thing that tells them apart. (Only the `with` form
; can reach this port — the reference reports a diagnostic on the other.)
;
; ★ The reference also carries `MultiLine bool`, a formatting hint the
; yardstick cannot see and nothing here reads — left out with the same
; statement ArrayLiteralExpression's MultiLine gets, rather than silently.
define ImportAttributesData
(
    token: int
    attributes: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
)

define ImportAttributeData
(
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    value: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ★ modifiers, [type], expression — the bracketed slot is the JSDoc
; reparser's, exactly as FunctionDeclaration's FullSignature is:
; NewExportAssignment is called with nil for it at its one parse-path site.
; `export = x` and `export default x` are one kind, so which word was written
; rides as a field.
define ExportAssignmentData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    is_export_equals: bool
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
)

define NamespaceExportDeclarationData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
)

; NOT ImportDeclarationData, although four of the five slots line up: the
; reference's ExportDeclaration carries IsTypeOnly and ImportDeclaration does
; not (`import type x from "m"` puts the phase on the CLAUSE instead). The
; §3.5n rule again — read both structs, share only on an identical list.
define ExportDeclarationData
(
    modifiers: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    is_type_only: bool
    export_clause: pointer[AstNode]
    module_specifier: pointer[AstNode]
    attributes: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ── slice 9: the loop and branch statements ─────────────────────────────────
;
; ★★★ A RULE THIS SLICE HAD TO STATE, because `do` and `while` are the case
; that forces it: the reference gives both of them the SAME two slots — an
; expression and a controlled statement, out of IterationStatementBase plus
; one field — and visits them in OPPOSITE orders (`do` runs its body before it
; evaluates the condition, and ForEachChild says so). §3.5n's test is that the
; slot LIST is identical, and an order is part of a list. So the invariant here
; is stronger than "same fields ⇒ share": **a record's field order IS its visit
; order**, which is what makes a child_at arm checkable line by line against
; ast_generated.go. `do` therefore gets its own record even though its fields
; are `while`'s two, and WithStatement shares `while`'s because its order
; matches as well as its fields.
define DoStatementData
(
    statement: pointer[AstNode]
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
)

; WhileStatement and WithStatement: expression, then statement. The name is the
; shape rather than either node, the way WrappedTypeData and ElementListData
; are named — see the rule above.
define ControlledStatementData
(
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
    statement: pointer[AstNode]
)

define ForStatementData
(
    initializer: pointer[AstNode]
    condition: pointer[AstNode]
    incrementor: pointer[AstNode]
    statement: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ForInStatement and ForOfStatement are ONE reference struct
; (ForInOrOfStatement), so this is the §3.5n check passing rather than a
; resemblance. `await_modifier` is only ever present on the `of` form — the
; reference builds the `in` form with nil for it — but the slot belongs to the
; struct, not to the kind.
define ForInOrOfStatementData
(
    await_modifier: pointer[AstNode]
    initializer: pointer[AstNode]
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
    statement: pointer[AstNode]
)

; BreakStatement and ContinueStatement: one optional label, and the
; reference's two structs are field for field the same.
;
; ★ The slot is `label_name`, not `label`: `label` is a RESERVED WORD in Scaly
; and it bites a STRUCTURE PROPERTY exactly as §3.5d found it biting a
; parameter — the parse fails at the property's own column with
; `expected ')'`, saying nothing about reservation, so it reads as a
; mis-balanced record. The root CLAUDE.md lists `label` among the words that
; cannot be BINDING names; the rule is wider than that list's wording.
define BreakOrContinueStatementData (label_name: pointer[AstNode])

define LabeledStatementData
(
    label_name: pointer[AstNode]
    statement: pointer[AstNode]
)

define SwitchStatementData
(
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
    case_block: pointer[AstNode]
)

; CaseClause and DefaultClause are ONE reference struct (CaseOrDefaultClause).
; The expression is absent on the default form, which is the same
; "null MEANS something here" the ReturnStatementData note is about — but it
; is one struct upstream, so the two arms share the record and the KIND is
; what says whether the slot can be filled.
define CaseOrDefaultClauseData
(
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
    statements: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
)

define TryStatementData
(
    try_block: pointer[AstNode]
    catch_clause: pointer[AstNode]
    finally_block: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ★ NO jsdoc slot and no modifiers — and the absence of the jsdoc CALL in
; parse_catch_clause is the thing to preserve: it is the one clause-shaped node
; in the reference whose parse routine does not call withJSDoc, while every
; statement around it does. Ported as written.
define CatchClauseData
(
    variable_declaration: pointer[AstNode]
    block: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ── slice 10: the binding pattern ───────────────────────────────────────────
;
; ObjectBindingPattern and ArrayBindingPattern are ONE reference struct
; (BindingPattern, whose only field is the element list), so they share a
; record — and the record they share is ElementListData, which is the §3.5n
; test passing rather than a resemblance: one list and nothing else, the same
; reading CaseBlock and NamedImports are under. The KIND is what says which
; bracket was written.
;
; ★ The elements of the two are NOT the same node, though: an array pattern's
; are BindingElements with a null propertyName, an object pattern's may carry
; one. That difference lives in the element, not in the pattern, which is why
; one record serves both here.

; DotDotDotToken, PropertyName, name, Initializer — all four OPTIONAL, and all
; four null at once for an ELISION: `[, a]` gives the reference a
; zero-width BindingElement with nothing in it, not the OmittedExpression an
; array LITERAL's hole gets. Two node kinds for the same hole in two grammars,
; which is exactly the kind of thing a shared record would have hidden.
define BindingElementData
(
    dot_dot_dot_token: pointer[AstNode]
    property_name: pointer[AstNode]
    name: pointer[AstNode]
    initializer: pointer[AstNode]
)

; ── slice 11: the template family ───────────────────────────────────────────
;
; TemplateExpression and TemplateLiteralType are ONE record, and the §3.5n check
; is what says so rather than the resemblance: both reference structs are
; `Head *TemplateHeadNode` followed by `TemplateSpans *…List`, two slots in that
; order. The list's ELEMENT type differs (TemplateSpan against
; TemplateLiteralTypeSpan) and that difference is not expressible here — a list
; is an Array of AstNode either way — which is the same reading NamedImports and
; NamedExports already share ElementListData under, and ClassDeclaration and
; InterfaceDeclaration share ClassLikeData under.
define TemplateLiteralData
(
    head: pointer[AstNode]
    template_spans: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
)

; TemplateSpan and TemplateLiteralTypeSpan, likewise one record: two slots, in
; the same order, neither ever null. The reference names slot 0 `Expression` in
; the one and `Type` in the other, and a NAME is not part of the §3.5n test —
; WrappedTypeData has been shared by fourteen arms whose reference field names
; are all different since slice 3.
;
; ★ The `literal` slot is what the span LOOP reads: a span whose literal is a
; TemplateMiddle is followed by another span, and one whose literal is a
; TemplateTail ends the template. That is why template_span_literal exists as an
; accessor rather than the loop reaching for child index 1 — the index is only
; right while the expression slot happens to be non-null.
define TemplateSpanData
(
    expression: pointer[AstNode]
    literal: pointer[AstNode]
)

; tag, questionDotToken, typeArguments, template — in that order, and the
; type-argument LIST sits third, between two single slots.
define TaggedTemplateData
(
    tag: pointer[AstNode]
    question_dot_token: pointer[AstNode]
    type_arguments: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    template: pointer[AstNode]
)

define NodeData union
(
    Token: TokenData
    Identifier: IdentifierData
    StringLiteral: LiteralData
    NumericLiteral: LiteralData
    BigIntLiteral: LiteralData
    NoSubstitutionTemplateLiteral: LiteralData

    ; Parser slice 16. A leaf like its four neighbours: the reference stores the
    ; literal's text and its token flags in the node, and this port stores
    ; neither (§3.5q), so the record is the shared empty one.
    RegularExpressionLiteral: LiteralData

    SourceFile: SourceFileData
    Block: BlockData
    EmptyStatement: EmptyStatementData
    ExpressionStatement: ExpressionStatementData
    VariableStatement: VariableStatementData
    VariableDeclarationList: VariableDeclarationListData
    VariableDeclaration: VariableDeclarationData
    TypeAliasDeclaration: TypeAliasDeclarationData
    TypeParameter: TypeParameterData
    TypeReference: TypeReferenceData
    TypeQuery: TypeQueryData
    QualifiedName: QualifiedNameData
    IndexedAccessType: IndexedAccessTypeData
    ConditionalType: ConditionalTypeData
    TypePredicate: TypePredicateData
    NamedTupleMember: NamedTupleMemberData
    UnionType: TypeListData
    IntersectionType: TypeListData
    TupleType: TypeListData
    ArrayType: WrappedTypeData
    ParenthesizedType: WrappedTypeData
    TypeOperator: WrappedTypeData
    RestType: WrappedTypeData
    OptionalType: WrappedTypeData
    InferType: WrappedTypeData
    LiteralType: WrappedTypeData
    PrefixUnaryExpression: WrappedTypeData
    JSDocNullableType: WrappedTypeData
    JSDocNonNullableType: WrappedTypeData
    Parameter: ParameterData
    FunctionDeclaration: FunctionDeclarationData
    FunctionType: FunctionTypeData
    ConstructorType: ConstructorTypeData
    ReturnStatement: ReturnStatementData
    IfStatement: IfStatementData

    ; ── slice 5, appended at the END as the header asks ─────────────────────
    BinaryExpression: BinaryExpressionData
    ConditionalExpression: ConditionalExpressionData
    YieldExpression: YieldExpressionData
    PostfixUnaryExpression: WrappedTypeData
    DeleteExpression: WrappedTypeData
    TypeOfExpression: WrappedTypeData
    VoidExpression: WrappedTypeData
    AwaitExpression: WrappedTypeData
    TypeAssertionExpression: TypeAssertionData
    AsExpression: AsExpressionData
    SatisfiesExpression: AsExpressionData
    NonNullExpression: WrappedTypeData
    PropertyAccessExpression: PropertyAccessData
    ElementAccessExpression: ElementAccessData
    CallExpression: CallExpressionData
    NewExpression: NewExpressionData
    ExpressionWithTypeArguments: ExpressionWithTypeArgumentsData
    MetaProperty: WrappedTypeData
    ParenthesizedExpression: WrappedTypeData
    ArrayLiteralExpression: ElementListData
    ObjectLiteralExpression: ElementListData
    SpreadElement: WrappedTypeData
    SpreadAssignment: WrappedTypeData
    PropertyAssignment: PropertyAssignmentData
    ShorthandPropertyAssignment: ShorthandPropertyAssignmentData
    ComputedPropertyName: WrappedTypeData
    ArrowFunction: ArrowFunctionData
    FunctionExpression: FunctionExpressionData

    ; ── slice 6, appended at the END as the header asks ─────────────────────
    ClassDeclaration: ClassLikeData
    ClassExpression: ClassLikeData
    HeritageClause: HeritageClauseData
    MethodDeclaration: MethodDeclarationData
    PropertyDeclaration: PropertyDeclarationData
    ConstructorDeclaration: ConstructorDeclarationData
    GetAccessorDeclaration: AccessorDeclarationData
    SetAccessorDeclaration: AccessorDeclarationData
    ClassStaticBlockDeclaration: ClassStaticBlockDeclarationData
    IndexSignatureDeclaration: IndexSignatureDeclarationData

    ; `#name`. It has an arm of its own rather than being a Token for the same
    ; reason Identifier does: it carries TEXT in the reference, and the field
    ; this port defers is a field both of them will grow.
    PrivateIdentifier: IdentifierData

    ; ── slice 7, appended at the END as the header asks ─────────────────────
    ;
    ; Two of these reuse a slice-6 record because the reference's slot lists
    ; are IDENTICAL, field for field and in order — not because they are
    ; similar. InterfaceDeclaration is ClassLikeData (modifiers, name,
    ; typeParameters, heritageClauses, members) and PropertySignature is
    ; PropertyDeclarationData (modifiers, name, postfixToken, type,
    ; initializer). Check any future reuse against ast_generated.go the same
    ; way; MethodSignatureData is there because that check FAILED for it.
    TypeLiteral: TypeLiteralData
    CallSignature: SignatureDeclarationData
    ConstructSignature: SignatureDeclarationData
    MethodSignature: MethodSignatureData
    PropertySignature: PropertyDeclarationData
    InterfaceDeclaration: ClassLikeData
    EnumDeclaration: EnumDeclarationData
    EnumMember: EnumMemberData
    ModuleDeclaration: ModuleDeclarationData
    ModuleBlock: BlockData
    MappedType: MappedTypeData

    ; ── slice 8, appended at the END as the header asks ─────────────────────
    ;
    ; Five arms reuse an existing record, each checked against
    ; ast_generated.go the way §3.5n demands rather than by resemblance:
    ; NamespaceImport, NamespaceExport and ExternalModuleReference have
    ; exactly ONE child slot each (WrappedTypeData, the recurring one-child
    ; node — `inner` is the namespace's name and the reference's expression),
    ; and NamedImports and NamedExports have exactly one LIST each
    ; (ElementListData).
    ImportDeclaration: ImportDeclarationData
    ImportEqualsDeclaration: ImportEqualsDeclarationData
    ImportClause: ImportClauseData
    NamespaceImport: WrappedTypeData
    NamedImports: ElementListData
    ImportSpecifier: ImportOrExportSpecifierData
    ExternalModuleReference: WrappedTypeData
    ImportAttributes: ImportAttributesData
    ImportAttribute: ImportAttributeData
    ExportAssignment: ExportAssignmentData
    NamespaceExportDeclaration: NamespaceExportDeclarationData
    ExportDeclaration: ExportDeclarationData
    NamespaceExport: WrappedTypeData
    NamedExports: ElementListData
    ExportSpecifier: ImportOrExportSpecifierData

    ; ── slice 9, appended at the END as the header asks ─────────────────────
    ;
    ; Three arms reuse an existing record, each checked against
    ; ast_generated.go rather than by resemblance:
    ;
    ;   WithStatement    ControlledStatementData — WhileStatement's two slots
    ;                    in WhileStatement's order (see that record's header
    ;                    for why `do` does NOT join them)
    ;   CaseBlock        ElementListData — one list and nothing else, the same
    ;                    reading NamedImports and the array literal are under
    ;   ThrowStatement   ExpressionStatementData — one expression slot that is
    ;                    never null. That is the distinction the
    ;                    ReturnStatementData note draws from the other side:
    ;                    `return;` has no expression, so it needs a record
    ;                    where null MEANS something, while `throw` on its own
    ;                    line gets a zero-width MISSING identifier rather than
    ;                    a null (measured against the reference — the node is
    ;                    there, spanning nothing).
    ;
    ; ★ DebuggerStatement gets NO arm and no record: it carries no field and no
    ; child, so it is a `Token` whose KIND says which it is — exactly the
    ; reading OmittedExpression and SemicolonClassElement are under (see the
    ; header). EmptyStatement, from slice 1, predates that note and keeps its
    ; own arm; the two are not in conflict, one is just older.
    DoStatement: DoStatementData
    WhileStatement: ControlledStatementData
    WithStatement: ControlledStatementData
    ForStatement: ForStatementData
    ForInStatement: ForInOrOfStatementData
    ForOfStatement: ForInOrOfStatementData
    BreakStatement: BreakOrContinueStatementData
    ContinueStatement: BreakOrContinueStatementData
    LabeledStatement: LabeledStatementData
    SwitchStatement: SwitchStatementData
    CaseBlock: ElementListData
    CaseClause: CaseOrDefaultClauseData
    DefaultClause: CaseOrDefaultClauseData
    ThrowStatement: ExpressionStatementData
    TryStatement: TryStatementData
    CatchClause: CatchClauseData

    ; slice 10 — see the two records above for why the patterns share and the
    ; element does not.
    ObjectBindingPattern: ElementListData
    ArrayBindingPattern: ElementListData
    BindingElement: BindingElementData

    ; ── slice 11, appended at the END as the header asks ────────────────────
    ;
    ; The three template-literal-like TOKENS get arms of their own rather than
    ; being `Token`, for the reason Identifier and PrivateIdentifier have theirs:
    ; the reference gives each of them Text, RawText and TemplateFlags, so the
    ; field this port defers is a field all of them will grow. They join
    ; NoSubstitutionTemplateLiteral, which is the fourth member of the
    ; reference's own TemplateLiteralLikeNode group and has been on LiteralData
    ; since slice 1. None of the four has a child.
    TemplateHead: LiteralData
    TemplateMiddle: LiteralData
    TemplateTail: LiteralData

    TemplateExpression: TemplateLiteralData
    TemplateSpan: TemplateSpanData
    TaggedTemplateExpression: TaggedTemplateData
    TemplateLiteralType: TemplateLiteralData
    TemplateLiteralTypeSpan: TemplateSpanData

    ; ── slice 12, appended at the END as the header asks ────────────────────
    ;
    ; ONE arm, and it shares WrappedTypeData for the reason §3.5n gives: the
    ; reference's `Decorator` is `Expression *LeftHandSideExpression` and
    ; nothing else, so the slot list is one slot and the order is trivially the
    ; same. The slot's NAME differs, which is explicitly not part of that test —
    ; the fourteen arms already on this record are called Type, Expression,
    ; Operand and Name.
    ;
    ; A decorator is a MODIFIER as far as every carrier is concerned: it goes
    ; into the same `modifiers` list a `export`/`declare`/`static` keyword goes
    ; into, so no carrying node needed a new slot for this slice and no arm
    ; below changed. That is the reference's own shape (ModifierList holds both,
    ; and `Node.Decorators()` is a FILTER over it), not a simplification.
    Decorator: WrappedTypeData

    ; ── slice 13c, appended at the END as the header asks ───────────────────
    ;
    ; ONE arm, and it is a node this port could not build before it had
    ; diagnostics: MissingDeclaration is what the reference leaves behind when
    ; modifiers or decorators promised a declaration that never arrived —
    ; `@d;`, `export = ;`, a decorated non-class expression. It always follows
    ; a report (Declaration_expected or Expression_expected), which is why it
    ; arrives with them.
    ;
    ; It shares ElementListData for the §3.5n reason: the reference's struct is
    ; StatementBase + DeclarationBase + ModifiersBase, i.e. exactly one slot,
    ; and `ForEachChild` is `visitModifiers(v, node.modifiers)` and nothing
    ; else. One list, one order — the same reading CaseBlock, NamedImports and
    ; the two binding patterns are under. The slot's NAME is `modifiers` rather
    ; than `elements`, which that test explicitly does not look at.
    MissingDeclaration: ElementListData
)

define AstNode
(
    kind: int
    flags: int

    ; The reference's core.TextRange, spelled out. `pos` is the FULL start —
    ; leading trivia included — and `end` is where the token ended. Keeping them
    ; two ints rather than a nested by-value struct is deliberate: a by-value
    ; struct nested in a struct is not laid out in a root that never declared it
    ; (exit 16), and this type is read from a program root.
    pos: int
    end: int

    data: NodeData
)
{
    function alloc(host: pointer[Page]) returns pointer[AstNode]
        host.allocate(sizeof AstNode, alignof AstNode) as pointer[AstNode]

    ; The reference's NodeList. It carries its own TextRange, which this port
    ; does not keep yet — nothing reads a list's extent, and the AST yardstick
    ; cannot see one either (ForEachChild visits a list's ELEMENTS, never the
    ; list). Stated because a hidden distinction hides every bug in it.
    function new_node_list(host: pointer[Page]) returns pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    {
        let a host.allocate(sizeof Array[pointer[AstNode]], alignof Array[pointer[AstNode]]) as pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
        set *a: Array[pointer[AstNode]]()
        a
    }

    ; ── accessors ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ;
    ; Statics taking the node by pointer, not `this` methods: a user program
    ; calling a CROSS-PACKAGE free function with a concept-pointer parameter
    ; fails resolution, while a concept STATIC resolves (root CLAUDE.md). The
    ; dumper is such a program.

    function kind_of(n: pointer[AstNode]) returns int
        n.kind

    function flags_of(n: pointer[AstNode]) returns int
        n.flags

    ; The SourceFile's diagnostic list, read through the node exactly as its
    ; children are — see SourceFileData. Answers 0 / false for any other kind,
    ; which is what the dump wants: only a SourceFile has them.
    function diagnostic_count(n: pointer[AstNode]) returns int
    {
        if n = null
            return 0
        choose n.data
            when f: SourceFile
            {
                if f.diagnostics = null
                    return 0
                return f.diagnostics.length()
            }
        0
    }

    function diagnostic_at(n: pointer[AstNode], i: int, out_pos: pointer[int], out_end: pointer[int], out_code: pointer[int]) returns bool
    {
        if n = null
            return false
        choose n.data
            when f: SourceFile
            {
                if f.diagnostics = null
                    return false
                return f.diagnostics.at(i, out_pos, out_end, out_code)
            }
        false
    }

    function pos_of(n: pointer[AstNode]) returns int
        n.pos

    function end_of(n: pointer[AstNode]) returns int
        n.end

    ; ── two payload questions the parser has to ask ─────────────────────────
    ;
    ; Both exist because the payload is a UNION and `choose` lives here, with
    ; the arms. The alternative — reaching into the payload from parser.scaly —
    ; would put a second copy of the arm list in a file that has no reason to
    ; know one.

    ; The operator of a BinaryExpression, or KindUnknown for anything else.
    ; parseBinaryExpressionRest needs it to decide how far an `as` may reach.
    function binary_operator_kind(n: pointer[AstNode]) returns int
    {
        if n = null
            return KindUnknown
        choose n.data
            when be: BinaryExpression
                return kind_of(be.operator_token)
        KindUnknown
    }

    ; The type argument LIST of an ExpressionWithTypeArguments — the one child
    ; slot that is a list and that a caller has to move rather than walk, when
    ; `f<T>(x)` is folded back from two nodes into one CallExpression.
    function type_arguments_of(n: pointer[AstNode]) returns pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]
    {
        if n = null
            return null
        choose n.data
            when e: ExpressionWithTypeArguments
                return e.type_arguments
        null
    }

    ; The LITERAL slot of a template span, which is what ends the span loop:
    ; parseTemplateSpans keeps going while `span.Literal.Kind == TemplateMiddle`
    ; and stops on a TemplateTail. It is an accessor rather than child_at(n, 1)
    ; because that index is only the literal while the expression slot is
    ; non-null — child_at SKIPS nulls, so a degenerate span would silently
    ; answer the literal at index 0 and the loop would read its own tail as an
    ; expression.
    function template_span_literal(n: pointer[AstNode]) returns pointer[AstNode]
    {
        if n = null
            return null
        choose n.data
            when ts: TemplateSpan
                return ts.literal
            when tlts: TemplateLiteralTypeSpan
                return tlts.literal
        null
    }

    ; The kind of an ImportEqualsDeclaration's MODULE REFERENCE, or
    ; KindUnknown for any other node. `isAnExternalModuleIndicatorNode` asks
    ; exactly this — an `import x = require("m")` makes the file a module while
    ; an `import x = A.B` does not — and asking it by child INDEX would be
    ; wrong the moment the declaration carries a modifier.
    function import_equals_reference_kind(n: pointer[AstNode]) returns int
    {
        if n = null
            return KindUnknown
        choose n.data
            when ie: ImportEqualsDeclaration
                return kind_of(ie.module_reference)
        KindUnknown
    }

    ; ── children ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ;
    ; The reference's ForEachChild(v Visitor), as an index pair. The mapping is a
    ; deliberate one and belongs in the vocabulary: ForEachChild takes a
    ; CALLBACK, and Scaly's only escaping-closure form is `return \x: …` — a
    ; recursive walk that builds a fresh closure per level is exactly the shape
    ; the escape checker exists to reject. An index pair needs no callback, and
    ; it lets the walk live in the caller, where the recursion is plain.
    ;
    ; ★ THE ORDER IS PART OF WHAT THE YARDSTICK COMPARES. Each arm below lists
    ; its slots in the reference's own ForEachChild order; a port that visits a
    ; node's children in a different order is a different tree and the dump says
    ; so. The slot lists are transcribed from ast_generated.go, not inferred.
    ;
    ; Null slots are SKIPPED, exactly as `visit(v, node.X)` skips a nil — so the
    ; i-th child is the i-th PRESENT one, and `child_count` is where the skipping
    ; stops. Both functions walk the same slot list for that reason: two
    ; independent switches would be two places to get the order wrong.

    function child_count(n: pointer[AstNode]) returns int
    {
        var i 0
        while child_at(n, i) <> null
            set i: i + 1
        i
    }

    ; ── the two slot shapes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ;
    ; The reference's ForEachChild body is a chain of `visit(v, node.X)` and
    ; `visitNodeList(v, node.Xs)`, each of which SKIPS a nil. These two pairs are
    ; that chain, read by index: ask the slot for its i-th child, and if it has
    ; none, subtract what it did contribute and ask the next.
    ;
    ; Writing it this way rather than open-coding each arm is not tidiness. A
    ; four-slot node open-coded is twenty lines of near-identical cursor
    ; arithmetic, and the ORDER of those lines is the thing the yardstick
    ; compares — a transcription error there is a different tree. Two lines per
    ; slot keeps the arm readable AGAINST ast_generated.go, which is how it is
    ; checked.

    function child_slot(n: pointer[AstNode], i: int) returns pointer[AstNode]
    {
        if n = null
            return null
        if i = 0
            return n
        null
    }

    function slot_count(n: pointer[AstNode]) returns int
    {
        if n = null
            return 0
        1
    }

    function child_in_list(a: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]], i: int) returns pointer[AstNode]
    {
        if a = null
            return null
        if i < a.get_length() as int
            return *(a.get_buffer() + i)
        null
    }

    function list_count(a: pointer[Array[pointer[AstNode]]]) returns int
    {
        if a = null
            return 0
        a.get_length() as int
    }

    function child_at(n: pointer[AstNode], i: int) returns pointer[AstNode]
    {
        choose n.data

            ; SourceFile: statements, then the end-of-file token.
            when f: SourceFile
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(f.statements, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(f.statements)
                return child_slot(f.end_of_file_token, k)
            }

            when b: Block
                return child_in_list(b.statements, i)

            when e: ExpressionStatement
                return child_slot(e.expression, i)

            when rs: ReturnStatement
                return child_slot(rs.expression, i)

            ; expression, thenStatement, elseStatement.
            when ifs: IfStatement
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(ifs.expression, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(ifs.expression)
                let b child_slot(ifs.then_statement, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(ifs.then_statement)
                return child_slot(ifs.else_statement, k)
            }

            ; VariableStatement: the modifier list, then the declaration list.
            ; The modifiers come FIRST — visitModifiers before visit(DeclarationList)
            ; in the reference — and they are ordinary nodes here, one Token per
            ; keyword, so `export declare var x` shows two children before the
            ; list.
            when v: VariableStatement
            {
                var k i
                let m child_in_list(v.modifiers, k)
                if m <> null
                    return m
                set k: k - list_count(v.modifiers)
                return child_slot(v.declaration_list, k)
            }

            when l: VariableDeclarationList
                return child_in_list(l.declarations, i)

            ; name, exclamationToken, type, initializer — in that order.
            when d: VariableDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(d.name, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(d.name)
                let b child_slot(d.exclamation_token, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(d.exclamation_token)
                let c child_slot(d.type_node, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(d.type_node)
                return child_slot(d.initializer, k)
            }

            ; ── the type surface ────────────────────────────────────────────
            ;
            ; modifiers, name, typeParameters, type.
            when ta: TypeAliasDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(ta.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(ta.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(ta.name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(ta.name)
                let c child_in_list(ta.type_parameters, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - list_count(ta.type_parameters)
                return child_slot(ta.type_node, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, name, constraint, expression, defaultType.
            when tp: TypeParameter
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(tp.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(tp.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(tp.name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(tp.name)
                let c child_slot(tp.constraint, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(tp.constraint)
                let d child_slot(tp.expression, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - slot_count(tp.expression)
                return child_slot(tp.default_type, k)
            }

            when tr: TypeReference
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(tr.type_name, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(tr.type_name)
                return child_in_list(tr.type_arguments, k)
            }

            when tq: TypeQuery
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(tq.expr_name, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(tq.expr_name)
                return child_in_list(tq.type_arguments, k)
            }

            when qn: QualifiedName
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(qn.left, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(qn.left)
                return child_slot(qn.right, k)
            }

            when ia: IndexedAccessType
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(ia.object_type, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(ia.object_type)
                return child_slot(ia.index_type, k)
            }

            when ct: ConditionalType
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(ct.check_type, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(ct.check_type)
                let b child_slot(ct.extends_type, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(ct.extends_type)
                let c child_slot(ct.true_type, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(ct.true_type)
                return child_slot(ct.false_type, k)
            }

            when pr: TypePredicate
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(pr.asserts_modifier, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(pr.asserts_modifier)
                let b child_slot(pr.parameter_name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(pr.parameter_name)
                return child_slot(pr.type_node, k)
            }

            when nt: NamedTupleMember
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(nt.dot_dot_dot_token, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(nt.dot_dot_dot_token)
                let b child_slot(nt.name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(nt.name)
                let c child_slot(nt.question_token, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(nt.question_token)
                return child_slot(nt.type_node, k)
            }

            ; ── signatures ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
            ;
            ; modifiers, dotDotDotToken, name, questionToken, type, initializer.
            when pd: Parameter
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(pd.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(pd.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(pd.dot_dot_dot_token, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(pd.dot_dot_dot_token)
                let c child_slot(pd.name, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(pd.name)
                let d child_slot(pd.question_token, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - slot_count(pd.question_token)
                let e child_slot(pd.type_node, k)
                if e <> null
                    return e
                set k: k - slot_count(pd.type_node)
                return child_slot(pd.initializer, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, asteriskToken, name, typeParameters, parameters, type,
            ; [fullSignature — see the record], body.
            when fd: FunctionDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(fd.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(fd.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(fd.asterisk_token, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(fd.asterisk_token)
                let c child_slot(fd.name, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(fd.name)
                let d child_in_list(fd.type_parameters, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - list_count(fd.type_parameters)
                let e child_in_list(fd.parameters, k)
                if e <> null
                    return e
                set k: k - list_count(fd.parameters)
                let f child_slot(fd.type_node, k)
                if f <> null
                    return f
                set k: k - slot_count(fd.type_node)
                return child_slot(fd.body, k)
            }

            ; typeParameters, parameters, type.
            when ft: FunctionType
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(ft.type_parameters, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(ft.type_parameters)
                let b child_in_list(ft.parameters, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - list_count(ft.parameters)
                return child_slot(ft.type_node, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, typeParameters, parameters, type.
            when cs: ConstructorType
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(cs.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(cs.modifiers)
                let b child_in_list(cs.type_parameters, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - list_count(cs.type_parameters)
                let c child_in_list(cs.parameters, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - list_count(cs.parameters)
                return child_slot(cs.type_node, k)
            }

            when ut: UnionType
                return child_in_list(ut.types, i)
            when it: IntersectionType
                return child_in_list(it.types, i)
            when tt: TupleType
                return child_in_list(tt.types, i)

            ; The one-child type nodes. Same shape, distinct kinds.
            when at: ArrayType
                return child_slot(at.inner, i)
            when pt: ParenthesizedType
                return child_slot(pt.inner, i)
            when ot: TypeOperator
                return child_slot(ot.inner, i)
            when rt: RestType
                return child_slot(rt.inner, i)
            when opt: OptionalType
                return child_slot(opt.inner, i)
            when inf: InferType
                return child_slot(inf.inner, i)
            when lt: LiteralType
                return child_slot(lt.inner, i)
            when pu: PrefixUnaryExpression
                return child_slot(pu.inner, i)
            when jn: JSDocNullableType
                return child_slot(jn.inner, i)
            when jnn: JSDocNonNullableType
                return child_slot(jnn.inner, i)

            ; ── the expression ladder ───────────────────────────────────────
            ;
            ; left, [type], operatorToken, right — the bracketed slot is the
            ; JSDoc reparser's and is never filled on the parse path (see the
            ; record).
            when be: BinaryExpression
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(be.left, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(be.left)
                let b child_slot(be.operator_token, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(be.operator_token)
                return child_slot(be.right, k)
            }

            ; condition, questionToken, whenTrue, colonToken, whenFalse. The two
            ; punctuation tokens ARE children — dropping them would shift every
            ; index after them.
            when ce: ConditionalExpression
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(ce.condition, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(ce.condition)
                let b child_slot(ce.question_token, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(ce.question_token)
                let c child_slot(ce.when_true, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(ce.when_true)
                let d child_slot(ce.colon_token, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - slot_count(ce.colon_token)
                return child_slot(ce.when_false, k)
            }

            when ye: YieldExpression
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(ye.asterisk_token, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(ye.asterisk_token)
                return child_slot(ye.expression, k)
            }

            ; expression, then type — the opposite order to TypeAssertion below.
            when ae: AsExpression
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(ae.expression, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(ae.expression)
                return child_slot(ae.type_node, k)
            }

            when se: SatisfiesExpression
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(se.expression, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(se.expression)
                return child_slot(se.type_node, k)
            }

            ; type, then expression.
            when tas: TypeAssertionExpression
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(tas.type_node, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(tas.type_node)
                return child_slot(tas.expression, k)
            }

            when pa: PropertyAccessExpression
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(pa.expression, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(pa.expression)
                let b child_slot(pa.question_dot_token, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(pa.question_dot_token)
                return child_slot(pa.name, k)
            }

            when ea: ElementAccessExpression
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(ea.expression, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(ea.expression)
                let b child_slot(ea.question_dot_token, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(ea.question_dot_token)
                return child_slot(ea.argument_expression, k)
            }

            when call: CallExpression
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(call.expression, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(call.expression)
                let b child_slot(call.question_dot_token, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(call.question_dot_token)
                let c child_in_list(call.type_arguments, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - list_count(call.type_arguments)
                return child_in_list(call.arguments, k)
            }

            when ne: NewExpression
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(ne.expression, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(ne.expression)
                let b child_in_list(ne.type_arguments, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - list_count(ne.type_arguments)
                return child_in_list(ne.arguments, k)
            }

            when ewta: ExpressionWithTypeArguments
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(ewta.expression, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(ewta.expression)
                return child_in_list(ewta.type_arguments, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, typeParameters, parameters, type, [fullSignature],
            ; equalsGreaterThanToken, body.
            when af: ArrowFunction
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(af.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(af.modifiers)
                let b child_in_list(af.type_parameters, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - list_count(af.type_parameters)
                let c child_in_list(af.parameters, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - list_count(af.parameters)
                let d child_slot(af.type_node, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - slot_count(af.type_node)
                let e child_slot(af.equals_greater_than_token, k)
                if e <> null
                    return e
                set k: k - slot_count(af.equals_greater_than_token)
                return child_slot(af.body, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, asteriskToken, name, typeParameters, parameters, type,
            ; [fullSignature], body — the same list the declaration has.
            when fe: FunctionExpression
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(fe.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(fe.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(fe.asterisk_token, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(fe.asterisk_token)
                let c child_slot(fe.name, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(fe.name)
                let d child_in_list(fe.type_parameters, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - list_count(fe.type_parameters)
                let e child_in_list(fe.parameters, k)
                if e <> null
                    return e
                set k: k - list_count(fe.parameters)
                let f child_slot(fe.type_node, k)
                if f <> null
                    return f
                set k: k - slot_count(fe.type_node)
                return child_slot(fe.body, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, name, postfixToken, [type], initializer.
            when pas: PropertyAssignment
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(pas.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(pas.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(pas.name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(pas.name)
                let c child_slot(pas.postfix_token, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(pas.postfix_token)
                return child_slot(pas.initializer, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, name, postfixToken, [type], equalsToken,
            ; objectAssignmentInitializer.
            when spa: ShorthandPropertyAssignment
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(spa.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(spa.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(spa.name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(spa.name)
                let c child_slot(spa.postfix_token, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(spa.postfix_token)
                let d child_slot(spa.equals_token, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - slot_count(spa.equals_token)
                return child_slot(spa.object_assignment_initializer, k)
            }

            when al: ArrayLiteralExpression
                return child_in_list(al.elements, i)
            when ol: ObjectLiteralExpression
                return child_in_list(ol.elements, i)

            ; The one-child expression nodes. Same shape, distinct kinds — the
            ; same grouping the type side uses.
            when pxu: PostfixUnaryExpression
                return child_slot(pxu.inner, i)
            when de: DeleteExpression
                return child_slot(de.inner, i)
            when toe: TypeOfExpression
                return child_slot(toe.inner, i)
            when ve: VoidExpression
                return child_slot(ve.inner, i)
            when awe: AwaitExpression
                return child_slot(awe.inner, i)
            when nne: NonNullExpression
                return child_slot(nne.inner, i)
            when mp: MetaProperty
                return child_slot(mp.inner, i)
            when pe: ParenthesizedExpression
                return child_slot(pe.inner, i)
            when sp: SpreadElement
                return child_slot(sp.inner, i)
            when spd: SpreadAssignment
                return child_slot(spd.inner, i)
            when cpn: ComputedPropertyName
                return child_slot(cpn.inner, i)

            ; ── the class family ────────────────────────────────────────────
            ;
            ; modifiers, name, typeParameters, heritageClauses, members — the
            ; declaration and the expression share the list AND the record.

            when cd: ClassDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(cd.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(cd.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(cd.name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(cd.name)
                let c child_in_list(cd.type_parameters, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - list_count(cd.type_parameters)
                let d child_in_list(cd.heritage_clauses, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - list_count(cd.heritage_clauses)
                return child_in_list(cd.members, k)
            }

            when ce: ClassExpression
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(ce.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(ce.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(ce.name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(ce.name)
                let c child_in_list(ce.type_parameters, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - list_count(ce.type_parameters)
                let d child_in_list(ce.heritage_clauses, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - list_count(ce.heritage_clauses)
                return child_in_list(ce.members, k)
            }

            ; The clause visits only its TYPES; `extends` vs `implements` is a
            ; field, not a child (see the record).
            when hc: HeritageClause
                return child_in_list(hc.types, i)

            ; modifiers, asteriskToken, name, postfixToken, typeParameters,
            ; parameters, type, [fullSignature], body.
            when md: MethodDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(md.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(md.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(md.asterisk_token, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(md.asterisk_token)
                let c child_slot(md.name, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(md.name)
                let d child_slot(md.postfix_token, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - slot_count(md.postfix_token)
                let e child_in_list(md.type_parameters, k)
                if e <> null
                    return e
                set k: k - list_count(md.type_parameters)
                let f child_in_list(md.parameters, k)
                if f <> null
                    return f
                set k: k - list_count(md.parameters)
                let g child_slot(md.type_node, k)
                if g <> null
                    return g
                set k: k - slot_count(md.type_node)
                return child_slot(md.body, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, name, postfixToken, type, initializer.
            when prd: PropertyDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(prd.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(prd.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(prd.name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(prd.name)
                let c child_slot(prd.postfix_token, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(prd.postfix_token)
                let d child_slot(prd.type_node, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - slot_count(prd.type_node)
                return child_slot(prd.initializer, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, typeParameters, parameters, type, [fullSignature],
            ; body — no name slot at all.
            when ctd: ConstructorDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(ctd.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(ctd.modifiers)
                let b child_in_list(ctd.type_parameters, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - list_count(ctd.type_parameters)
                let c child_in_list(ctd.parameters, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - list_count(ctd.parameters)
                let d child_slot(ctd.type_node, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - slot_count(ctd.type_node)
                return child_slot(ctd.body, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, name, typeParameters, parameters, type,
            ; [fullSignature], body — the getter and the setter share it.
            when ga: GetAccessorDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(ga.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(ga.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(ga.name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(ga.name)
                let c child_in_list(ga.type_parameters, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - list_count(ga.type_parameters)
                let d child_in_list(ga.parameters, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - list_count(ga.parameters)
                let e child_slot(ga.type_node, k)
                if e <> null
                    return e
                set k: k - slot_count(ga.type_node)
                return child_slot(ga.body, k)
            }

            when sa: SetAccessorDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(sa.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(sa.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(sa.name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(sa.name)
                let c child_in_list(sa.type_parameters, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - list_count(sa.type_parameters)
                let d child_in_list(sa.parameters, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - list_count(sa.parameters)
                let e child_slot(sa.type_node, k)
                if e <> null
                    return e
                set k: k - slot_count(sa.type_node)
                return child_slot(sa.body, k)
            }

            when csb: ClassStaticBlockDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(csb.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(csb.modifiers)
                return child_slot(csb.body, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, parameters, type.
            when isd: IndexSignatureDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(isd.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(isd.modifiers)
                let b child_in_list(isd.parameters, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - list_count(isd.parameters)
                return child_slot(isd.type_node, k)
            }

            ; ── the type-member surface (slice 7) ───────────────────────────

            when tl: TypeLiteral
                return child_in_list(tl.members, i)

            ; typeParameters, parameters, type — for BOTH signature arms.
            when cs: CallSignature
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(cs.type_parameters, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(cs.type_parameters)
                let b child_in_list(cs.parameters, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - list_count(cs.parameters)
                return child_slot(cs.type_node, k)
            }

            when ks: ConstructSignature
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(ks.type_parameters, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(ks.type_parameters)
                let b child_in_list(ks.parameters, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - list_count(ks.parameters)
                return child_slot(ks.type_node, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, name, postfixToken, typeParameters, parameters, type.
            when ms: MethodSignature
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(ms.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(ms.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(ms.name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(ms.name)
                let c child_slot(ms.postfix_token, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(ms.postfix_token)
                let d child_in_list(ms.type_parameters, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - list_count(ms.type_parameters)
                let e child_in_list(ms.parameters, k)
                if e <> null
                    return e
                set k: k - list_count(ms.parameters)
                return child_slot(ms.type_node, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, name, postfixToken, type, initializer — the same slot
            ; list as PropertyDeclaration, which is why it shares the record.
            when ps: PropertySignature
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(ps.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(ps.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(ps.name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(ps.name)
                let c child_slot(ps.postfix_token, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(ps.postfix_token)
                let d child_slot(ps.type_node, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - slot_count(ps.type_node)
                return child_slot(ps.initializer, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, name, typeParameters, heritageClauses, members — the
            ; same slot list as a class, which is why it shares the record.
            when id: InterfaceDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(id.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(id.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(id.name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(id.name)
                let c child_in_list(id.type_parameters, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - list_count(id.type_parameters)
                let d child_in_list(id.heritage_clauses, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - list_count(id.heritage_clauses)
                return child_in_list(id.members, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, name, members.
            when ed: EnumDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(ed.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(ed.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(ed.name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(ed.name)
                return child_in_list(ed.members, k)
            }

            when em2: EnumMember
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(em2.name, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(em2.name)
                return child_slot(em2.initializer, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, name, body. `keyword` is a FIELD, not a child.
            when md: ModuleDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(md.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(md.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(md.name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(md.name)
                return child_slot(md.body, k)
            }

            when mb: ModuleBlock
                return child_in_list(mb.statements, i)

            ; readonlyToken, typeParameter, nameType, questionToken, type,
            ; members.
            when mt: MappedType
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(mt.readonly_token, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(mt.readonly_token)
                let b child_slot(mt.type_parameter, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(mt.type_parameter)
                let c child_slot(mt.name_type, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(mt.name_type)
                let d child_slot(mt.question_token, k)
                if d <> null
                    return d
                set k: k - slot_count(mt.question_token)
                let e child_slot(mt.type_node, k)
                if e <> null
                    return e
                set k: k - slot_count(mt.type_node)
                return child_in_list(mt.members, k)
            }

            ; ── the import and export declarations (slice 8) ────────────────
            ;
            ; modifiers, importClause, moduleSpecifier, attributes.
            when imd: ImportDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(imd.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(imd.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(imd.import_clause, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(imd.import_clause)
                let c child_slot(imd.module_specifier, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(imd.module_specifier)
                return child_slot(imd.attributes, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, name, moduleReference. `is_type_only` is a FIELD.
            when ie: ImportEqualsDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(ie.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(ie.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(ie.name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(ie.name)
                return child_slot(ie.module_reference, k)
            }

            ; name, namedBindings — no modifiers, and the phase modifier is a
            ; field rather than the token node it is written as.
            when ic: ImportClause
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(ic.name, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(ic.name)
                return child_slot(ic.named_bindings, k)
            }

            when nsi: NamespaceImport
                return child_slot(nsi.inner, i)
            when nis: NamedImports
                return child_in_list(nis.elements, i)
            when nse: NamespaceExport
                return child_slot(nse.inner, i)
            when nes: NamedExports
                return child_in_list(nes.elements, i)
            when emr: ExternalModuleReference
                return child_slot(emr.inner, i)

            ; propertyName, name — for BOTH specifier arms.
            when isp: ImportSpecifier
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(isp.property_name, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(isp.property_name)
                return child_slot(isp.name, k)
            }

            when esp: ExportSpecifier
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(esp.property_name, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(esp.property_name)
                return child_slot(esp.name, k)
            }

            when iats: ImportAttributes
                return child_in_list(iats.attributes, i)

            when iat: ImportAttribute
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(iat.name, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(iat.name)
                return child_slot(iat.value, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, [type], expression — the bracketed slot is the JSDoc
            ; reparser's (see the record).
            when ea2: ExportAssignment
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(ea2.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(ea2.modifiers)
                return child_slot(ea2.expression, k)
            }

            when ned: NamespaceExportDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(ned.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(ned.modifiers)
                return child_slot(ned.name, k)
            }

            ; modifiers, exportClause, moduleSpecifier, attributes.
            when exd: ExportDeclaration
            {
                var k i
                let a child_in_list(exd.modifiers, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - list_count(exd.modifiers)
                let b child_slot(exd.export_clause, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(exd.export_clause)
                let c child_slot(exd.module_specifier, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(exd.module_specifier)
                return child_slot(exd.attributes, k)
            }

            ; ── slice 9: the loop and branch statements ──────────────────────
            ;
            ; ★ statement, THEN expression — `do` is the one iteration form
            ; whose body is visited before its condition, and the record's field
            ; order says so (see DoStatementData's header). Reading this arm
            ; against WhileStatement's below is the whole check.
            when ds: DoStatement
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(ds.statement, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(ds.statement)
                return child_slot(ds.expression, k)
            }

            when ws: WhileStatement
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(ws.expression, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(ws.expression)
                return child_slot(ws.statement, k)
            }

            when wis: WithStatement
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(wis.expression, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(wis.expression)
                return child_slot(wis.statement, k)
            }

            ; initializer, condition, incrementor, statement — every one of the
            ; first three optional, which is what `for (;;) ;` is.
            when fs: ForStatement
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(fs.initializer, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(fs.initializer)
                let b child_slot(fs.condition, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(fs.condition)
                let c child_slot(fs.incrementor, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(fs.incrementor)
                return child_slot(fs.statement, k)
            }

            ; awaitModifier, initializer, expression, statement. Two arms, one
            ; reference struct — so the two slot lists cannot drift apart.
            when fis: ForInStatement
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(fis.await_modifier, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(fis.await_modifier)
                let b child_slot(fis.initializer, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(fis.initializer)
                let c child_slot(fis.expression, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(fis.expression)
                return child_slot(fis.statement, k)
            }

            when fos: ForOfStatement
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(fos.await_modifier, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(fos.await_modifier)
                let b child_slot(fos.initializer, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(fos.initializer)
                let c child_slot(fos.expression, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(fos.expression)
                return child_slot(fos.statement, k)
            }

            when bs: BreakStatement
                return child_slot(bs.label_name, i)

            when cs: ContinueStatement
                return child_slot(cs.label_name, i)

            when ls: LabeledStatement
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(ls.label_name, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(ls.label_name)
                return child_slot(ls.statement, k)
            }

            when ss: SwitchStatement
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(ss.expression, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(ss.expression)
                return child_slot(ss.case_block, k)
            }

            when cb: CaseBlock
                return child_in_list(cb.elements, i)

            ; expression, then the statement list. The expression is absent on
            ; the default clause and child_slot skips it, so a default clause's
            ; first child is its first statement.
            when cc: CaseClause
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(cc.expression, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(cc.expression)
                return child_in_list(cc.statements, k)
            }

            when dc: DefaultClause
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(dc.expression, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(dc.expression)
                return child_in_list(dc.statements, k)
            }

            when ts: ThrowStatement
                return child_slot(ts.expression, i)

            when trs: TryStatement
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(trs.try_block, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(trs.try_block)
                let b child_slot(trs.catch_clause, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(trs.catch_clause)
                return child_slot(trs.finally_block, k)
            }

            when cl: CatchClause
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(cl.variable_declaration, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(cl.variable_declaration)
                return child_slot(cl.block, k)
            }

            ; ── slice 10: the binding pattern ───────────────────────────────

            when obp: ObjectBindingPattern
                return child_in_list(obp.elements, i)
            when abp: ArrayBindingPattern
                return child_in_list(abp.elements, i)

            ; dotDotDotToken, propertyName, name, initializer — in that order.
            ; All four may be null, and an elision has all four null at once, so
            ; this arm answers null at i = 0 and the element is a LEAF that
            ; nevertheless exists. That is not a degenerate case to guard: it is
            ; what the reference builds for `[, a]`.
            when be: BindingElement
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(be.dot_dot_dot_token, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(be.dot_dot_dot_token)
                let b child_slot(be.property_name, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(be.property_name)
                let c child_slot(be.name, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - slot_count(be.name)
                return child_slot(be.initializer, k)
            }

            ; ── slice 11: the template family ───────────────────────────────
            ;
            ; head, then the span list — the same two slots for the expression
            ; and the type, which is why one record serves both (see its header).

            when te: TemplateExpression
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(te.head, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(te.head)
                return child_in_list(te.template_spans, k)
            }

            when tlt: TemplateLiteralType
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(tlt.head, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(tlt.head)
                return child_in_list(tlt.template_spans, k)
            }

            ; expression (or, in a type, the type), then the literal.
            when ts: TemplateSpan
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(ts.expression, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(ts.expression)
                return child_slot(ts.literal, k)
            }

            when tlts: TemplateLiteralTypeSpan
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(tlts.expression, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(tlts.expression)
                return child_slot(tlts.literal, k)
            }

            ; tag, questionDotToken, typeArguments, template — the list THIRD.
            when tt: TaggedTemplateExpression
            {
                var k i
                let a child_slot(tt.tag, k)
                if a <> null
                    return a
                set k: k - slot_count(tt.tag)
                let b child_slot(tt.question_dot_token, k)
                if b <> null
                    return b
                set k: k - slot_count(tt.question_dot_token)
                let c child_in_list(tt.type_arguments, k)
                if c <> null
                    return c
                set k: k - list_count(tt.type_arguments)
                return child_slot(tt.template, k)
            }

            ; ── slice 12: the decorator ─────────────────────────────────────
            ;
            ; One slot, `visit(v, node.Expression)`.
            when dec: Decorator
                return child_slot(dec.inner, i)

            ; ── slice 13c: the missing declaration ──────────────────────────
            ;
            ; One LIST slot, `visitModifiers(v, node.modifiers)`.
            when md: MissingDeclaration
                return child_in_list(md.elements, i)

            ; The leaves. The reference gives none of these a ForEachChild, so
            ; they inherit NodeDefault's `return false` — no children at all.
            ; `Token` covers the punctuation and keyword nodes AND, for the same
            ; reason, KeywordTypeNode and ThisTypeNode (see the header).
            when t: Token
                return null
            when d: Identifier
                return null
            when pid: PrivateIdentifier
                return null
            when s: StringLiteral
                return null
            when nu: NumericLiteral
                return null
            when bi: BigIntLiteral
                return null
            when ns: NoSubstitutionTemplateLiteral
                return null
            when re: RegularExpressionLiteral
                return null
            when th: TemplateHead
                return null
            when tm: TemplateMiddle
                return null
            when tl: TemplateTail
                return null
            when em: EmptyStatement
                return null

        null
    }
}
